   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Que»",
     "texto": [
      "The pronoun **que** (that) joins two sentences and points to a noun: **A casa que comprei é grande** (the house I bought is big). It's the most used relative in Portuguese, as in Spanish.",
      "It is used regardless of whether the noun is masculine, feminine, singular or plural: **o jardim que tens**, **as casas que vês**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Que» without preposition",
     "texto": [
      "If the relative clause needs no preposition, use **que**: **Esse jardim que vês ao fundo** (that garden you see at the back)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
